From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:50:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] room: Accept a V4L2 encoder without the frame-level rate control switch

InitControls() sets V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE first and fails
the session when that fails ("Failed enabling bitrate control"). The
control is mandatory for ChromeOS drivers, but Apple's AVE driver in the
7.3 edge kernel does not have it (the SmartRoom kernels up to sr22 added
it only to satisfy this check). On that kernel every encoder session
fails before the first frame, at any resolution, and WebRTC falls back
to OpenH264.

Set the control only when the device exposes it, as is done for the
optional controls around it. The driver runs its rate controller per
frame in the bitrate mode InitControls() sets next.

Room package only.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
@@ -2279,10 +2279,15 @@
 #endif
   );
 
-  // Enable frame-level bitrate control. This is the only mandatory control.
-  if (!device_->SetExtCtrls(
-          V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG,
-          {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE, 1)})) {
+  // Enable frame-level bitrate control. ChromeOS drivers expose it and it is
+  // mandatory for them. A driver that does not have the control (Apple's AVE
+  // in the 7.3 edge kernel) runs its rate controller on every frame in the
+  // bitrate mode that is set below, so the missing control is not an error.
+  if (!device_->IsCtrlExposed(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE)) {
+    DVLOGF(2) << "Device has no frame-level bitrate control switch";
+  } else if (!device_->SetExtCtrls(
+                 V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG,
+                 {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE, 1)})) {
     SetErrorState({EncoderStatus::Codes::kEncoderHardwareDriverError,
                    "Failed enabling bitrate control"});
     return false;
-- 
